{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": "Router-level cases both hosts must answer identically (plan 2026-11-16-mac-remote-control-phase1, T4). Bodies compare as parsed JSON; key order and escaping are not part of the contract. An absent hosts means both hosts; an absent expect.body is not compared; expect.errorPrefix replaces the check of body.error; expect.invocations is the exact list the fake surface received ([] = none, absent = not checked). surfaceReply defaults to {\"ok\":true}. Invariant: every action id in an http case for both hosts is supported on macOS when the case is added, or is in neither file (bogus, automation.magic); rows only move toward supported, so a case stays valid. Snapshot states keep their keys in sorted order (the Mac sorts nodes, Windows writes document order) and hold no secret-named key or redactable string, so Mac redaction is the identity there. ageMsNear allows +/-400 ms; 500 and 5000 sit at least 1500 ms from the 2000 ms stale boundary.",
